AArch64 to PPC

"MOV %r,&c" -> "li %r,&c"
"STR %r,[%a]" -> "stw %r,0(%a)"
"LDR %r,[%a]" -> "lwz %r,0(%a)"
"STLR %r,[%a]" -> "sync; stw %r,0(%a)"
"LDAR %r,[%a]" -> "sync; lwz %r,0(%a); lwsync"
"LDAPR %r,[%a]" -> "lwz %r,0(%a); lwsync"
"DMB SY" -> "sync"
"DMB LD" -> "lwsync"
# DMB ST is `sync`, not `lwsync`. lwsync orders store->store on the executing
# hart, which is all DMB ISHST asks for locally, but AArch64 barriers are also
# cumulative over coherence order and lwsync's cumulativity is not: see the
# CO-R shape that check.sh's two hand-built controls pin.
"DMB ST" -> "sync"
# LDXR..STXR fused onto the native reservation (TranslateExclusive.cpp,
# TryFuseExclusiveLoop). One rule per pair rather than one per instruction,
# because the lowering is one region: the leading fence is hoisted above the
# l*arx and shared by both halves, which no per-instruction rule could express.
#
# Modelled as a SINGLE attempt with its status materialised, not as the retry
# loop the JIT emits. That is deliberate and it is the faithful abstraction: the
# ordering structure of one pass is the ordering structure of every pass, and
# herd7 then explores the st*cx. failing exactly where AArch64 lets the STXR
# fail, so the two sides stay comparable. The `bne` is not an artefact either --
# CR0 is the only place POWER puts the status, so every real lowering branches
# on it, including the JIT's `bne-` back edge.
#
# The leading `sync` is what the model insists on. An `lwsync` there is unsound
# for the R shape (three tests), which settles the question OPTIMIZATION-CHECKLIST
# P7 left open: a release RMW cannot take lwsync on this mapping. Dropping the
# leading sync on the acquire side is unsound too, which is why LDAXR gets one.
"LDXR %r,[%a]; STXR W%s,W%v,[%a]" -> "lwarx %r,r0,%a; li %s,1; stwcx. %v,r0,%a; bne xd; li %s,0; xd:"
"LDAXR %r,[%a]; STXR W%s,W%v,[%a]" -> "sync; lwarx %r,r0,%a; lwsync; li %s,1; stwcx. %v,r0,%a; bne xd; li %s,0; xd:"
"LDXR %r,[%a]; STLXR W%s,W%v,[%a]" -> "sync; lwarx %r,r0,%a; li %s,1; stwcx. %v,r0,%a; bne xd; li %s,0; xd:"
"LDAXR %r,[%a]; STLXR W%s,W%v,[%a]" -> "sync; lwarx %r,r0,%a; lwsync; li %s,1; stwcx. %v,r0,%a; bne xd; li %s,0; xd:"
